{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791710854,"nonce":"Pfn0FEEniEF66MguQyDzTRKTekA=","message":"Slice 4 is on main and pushed, ending at 2b9896972059e19ab43e3b0c59e2d39e24e7fc6c. The field reload is 051a741f86a3c1bfe6967349b82773f1feed532e. The fixes from the reviews are 857c00fdda4a8daacc58dfc195123ee26f72bc63, 74b37236baab563b84de533e514850bff332dda9 and 2b9896972059e19ab43e3b0c59e2d39e24e7fc6c. A dropped field keeps its slot in 4785912f135eb50e85a268a094cbc0dac36faafe. 2ae27b832d025e54d24ed6090c76f852cfa214d2 fixes the clippy failure that slice 3 left on main.\n\nA reload now takes fields added to a class that no class extends, wherever they are in the source, and a field it drops stays in the class unused, so a removal or a rename reloads. Objects made before the reload hold zero in an added field, since the constructor's initialiser has not run for them. ashui's tests/fixtures/hotreload v2 to v8 reload under the default tiers, --jit-threshold 1, cranelift and llvm, and the unit corpus passes with --hot-reload on (1350 of 1350).\n\nHow: under --hot-reload every object is allocated with 64 spare bytes (ASH_RELOAD_ROOM). reload/fields.rs puts the new program's field list for a class in the running order with the added fields last and rewrites the field indexes in the bodies, so a body that did not change is the body that was running. A class cannot grow past the smallest object ever allocated of it, which is the size it had when it first grew plus the room, however many reloads add to it. The LLVM tier's sized and inline allocation is off under hot reload, so the size comes from the runtime.\n\nRefused, with the reason on stderr: a field of another type; a class that something extends, in either program; no room left; a class that a hl.CArray holds, when its size would change; a static added to a running class; a constructor that stores something other than a constant or null into an added field, or into one that comes back after being dropped, except an ashui __state field in a program that has ashui.ui.HotReload.stateOnFirstUse (built with -D ashui_hot_reload).\n\nFour read-only reviews found defects the gates had not, all fixed: a value that one branch of an if sets was taken for a constant (HL labels only backward jump targets, so a forward merge is invisible to a scan for labels), a class that implements two interfaces could never gain a field, a CArray of a class would change stride under a live array, Reflect.fields could write past the array it allocated while a reload replaced the field list, a register whose address is taken was taken for a constant, and a dropped field that came back skipped the constructor rule.\n\nLeft: 39dc5ead26032eb03529b8cd30f4527d3848b0dbe944510eb6c51f745f0649cd (the class lists are swapped without a lock the readers take); only the constructor's own body is read for an initialiser; an added field with a non-zero constant initialiser leaves older objects at zero; each dropped field keeps its bytes of the spare room, and a class that has dropped one cannot gain a subclass; the statics of a running class, which this issue stays open for. That includes the first use, or the last removal, of a standard library static that is written in Haxe, such as Reflect.setField: it adds or removes a binding of the $Reflect statics object and the reload is refused with \"$Reflect binds different statics\". A fixture met it when a version stopped calling setField.","files":null}]}